+# Lifecycle regression tests (no PS5)
+
+Production owner is `ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier`. A lease is memory-only per browser page; `generation` confirms a compare-and-swap prepare, and `X-PSRP-Lease` authorizes the corresponding peer/controller. Preparing never switches the receiver. `/webrtc/session/{id}/commit` requires a bound, actually connected server peer and switches under the host gate. Browser DELETE is not console stop. `/playstation/stop-session` is the explicit owner/current-controller operation.
+
+Configuration: `RemotePlay:BrowserGraceSeconds` / environment `RemotePlay__BrowserGraceSeconds`, default 60 (clamped 1–3600). Initial sessions without a valid browser and disconnected sessions expire; pending offers cannot renew this deadline. Cleanup checks once per second.
+
+## Local commands
+
+From `psrp/source`:
+
+```sh
+../sdk/dotnet run --project RemotePlay.RegressionTests
+# Optional isolated application STUN test; DNS/STUN only, no PS5:
+PSRP_RUN_STUN_INTEGRATION=1 ../sdk/dotnet run --project RemotePlay.RegressionTests -- network_real_application_ICE
+```
+
+The existing H264 regression requires Playwright/Chromium and Node `h264-profile-level-id`. In the current workspace use the staging `test-venv/bin` on PATH and `test-tools/node_modules:RemotePlay.Web/node_modules` on NODE_PATH. The default suite has 40 tests (the original 37 plus two receiver atomicity paths and one multi-tick slow cleanup); the network integration is opt-in, unchanged.
+
+Start these **test-only loopback processes** in separate terminals:
+
+```sh
+# Source root. New process required for each backend integration run.
+../sdk/dotnet run --project RemotePlay.RegressionTests -- --lifecycle-http-server
+# RemotePlay.Web:
+node node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js --host 127.0.0.1 --port 5187 --strictPort
+```
+
+Run the Python browser tests under the staging Playwright venv:
+
+- `browser_lifecycle_test.py`: native Chinese confirm/cancel against simulated API.
+- `browser_stale_async_test.py`: a delayed old start cannot overwrite the new lease.
+- `browser_hook_test.py`: real React hook/provider/UI, auto-connect, cancel and failed replacement, browser timers advanced 15 seconds, no discover/wake/stop calls before consent or during cleanup.
+- `browser_backend_integration.py`: real production services/API client, actual MVC/filter/EF permissions, real loopback Chromium↔SIPSorcery WebRTC and actual SignalR WebSockets; fake console session/media transport. It covers failed new answer retaining A, A→B→C preparation, stale generation, old HTTP/delete/SignalR input/disconnect, revoked UserDevice, same-peer release, reattach without console reconnect, and explicit stop of console TCP+media. The default fixture's PS5 start operation always throws; the explicitly selected fresh fixture only increments an in-memory fake-console counter. Test auth creates NameIdentifier claims only in this test executable, not in production.
+
+For PWA tests, serve the published staging `www` with `python tests/artifact_server.py /absolute/staging/www`, then run `browser_sw_test.py`. This test server substitutes harmless network counters for diagnostic/API navigation, so it never executes the retained diagnostic player's scripts.
+
+Do not run production Program or deploy these artifacts for these tests. Only the `RemotePlay` project is published; the fake host, fake authentication scheme and React harness are excluded from production artifacts.
+
+For Node 18 builds, enable the runtime's webcrypto global explicitly:
+
+```sh
+node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit
+node --experimental-global-webcrypto node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build
+```
+
+## Independent-review blocking fixes (no PS5)
+
+- `review_receiver_atomic_pipeline` / `review_receiver_atomic_legacy`: dedicated threads pause A removal at an existing log call inside the real route update, then attempt B installation. B must block until A leaves the entire receiver operation (not just its reference assignment). After joining, stream and pipeline/output or AVHandler routing references equal B; actual OutputPipeline audio (1 packet) / parsed AVHandler audio via its jitter buffer (6 packets) reach only B. A's later disconnect is harmless. The pause uses reflection to inject a logger into isolated real routing objects; no production test hook or console connection is added. Pre-fix code deterministically fails the overlapping-operation assertion even though this particular pause point is after its sink assignment.
